    {
      "text": "THE COLORED JONES POL YNOMIAL AND KONTSEVICH-ZAGIER SERIES FOR DOUBLE TWIST KNOTS — Using a result of Takata, we prove a formula for the colored Jones polynomial of the double twist knots K(−m,−p)\n\n**THE COLORED JONES POL YNOMIAL AND KONTSEVICH-ZAGIER SERIES FOR DOUBLE TWIST KNOTS**\n\n*JEREMY LOVEJOY AND ROBERT OSBURN*\n\n24 pp, 6 sections.\n\n**Abstract.** Using a result of Takata, we prove a formula for the colored Jones polynomial of the double twist knots K(−m,−p) and K(−m,p) where m and p are positive integers. In the ( −m, −p) case, this leads to new families of q-hypergeometric series generalizing the Kontsevich-Zagier series. Comparing with the cyclotomic expansion of the colored Jones polynomials of K(m,p) gives a generalization of a duality at roots of unity between the Kontsevich-Zagier function and the generating function for strongly unimodal sequences.\n\n**Outline.** 1 Introduction; 2 Preliminaries; 3 Proofs of Theorems 1.1 and 1.2; 4 Concluding remarks and questions; Acknowledgements; References\n\n**Extracted claims (proposals, not verified).**\n- Theorem 1.1: For positive integers m and p, we have\n- Theorem 1.2: For positive integers m and p, we have\n- Corollary 1.3: If ζN is any Nth root of unity, then we have\n- Corollary 1.4: If ζN is any Nth root of unity, then we have\n- Corollary 1.3: as a key illustration. Furthermore, we suspect that the generalized Kontsevich-\n- Lemma 2.2: Forl = 4mp− 1 and t = 4mp− 2p− 1, we have",
